1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:04,250
[KIVIA] Thanks to the hero unit
and their dragoon's attack,

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:07,380
we narrowly managed
to fend off the assassins.

3
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:10,800
Still, my network of deployed
Holy Knights was gutted,

4
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:13,010
and nearly half of them
perished.

5
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:16,770
It was a sneak attack designed
to isolate us and the goddess.

6
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:19,480
Their execution was flawless.

7
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,020
Sounds as if you're implying

8
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:23,230
that we might have a traitor
in our midst.

9
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:25,440
If we can't trust
our own allies,

10
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:27,440
we have no hope
of prevailing.

11
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:29,660
My sniper unit
was massacred.

12
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:31,530
Nearly all of them
were picked off.

13
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:33,030
[RAJIT] I suggest we limit

14
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:34,740
Goddess Teoritta's
protective detail

15
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:36,450
to only those we trust most.

16
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:38,000
-That way--
-I trust no one.

17
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:40,040
-[all gasp]
-[grunts]

18
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,540
The concept of "trust"

19
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:44,130
is downright laughable
at this point.

20
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:46,880
We should even be skeptical
of everyone in this room.

21
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:47,970
-[grunting]
-[Rajit scoffs]

22
00:00:48,010 --> 00:00:49,380
And I can't think of anyone

23
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:51,680
we should trust less
than a penal hero.

24
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:54,220
This at least warrants
an investigation.

25
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:55,930
You should contact
the Twelfth Order

26
00:00:55,970 --> 00:00:57,020
of the Holy Knights.

27
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:58,850
Though they specialize
in intelligence,

28
00:00:58,890 --> 00:01:01,310
they strictly remain hidden
from the public eye.

29
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:03,230
There's no chance
of winning this fight

30
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:04,900
if we don't know
who might betray us.

31
00:01:05,610 --> 00:01:07,650
Can we at least agree on that?

32
00:01:10,150 --> 00:01:12,240
After careful consideration

33
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,070
I'd like to solicit the opinion

34
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,280
of the special advisor
who has joined us today.

35
00:01:16,330 --> 00:01:19,620
High Priest Marlen,
what's your take?

36
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,500
[MARLEN] Hmm... fascinating.

37
00:01:22,790 --> 00:01:25,290
As I've only just arrived
from the First Capital,

38
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:27,000
it's difficult to say.

39
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:31,050
Who we can trust is a matter
of grave importance.

40
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:32,840
No one present
is above scrutiny,

41
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:33,970
including myself.

42
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:35,220
Yet, to be frank,

43
00:01:35,430 --> 00:01:38,310
I doubt the intelligence unit
will come to our aid.

44
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:41,140
How go the interrogations,
Patausche?

45
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:43,690
Not well, I am afraid.

46
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:45,310
Most of the thugs we took alive

47
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:48,400
were adventurers for hire
without any useful intel.

48
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:52,280
I regret that we failed
to capture the assassins.

49
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,240
Let's not despair.

50
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,280
You needn't shoulder the blame.

51
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,410
It isn't yours alone.

52
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:00,750
Try not to stew in
your own regret.

53
00:02:00,790 --> 00:02:02,830
It will not improve
our situation.

54
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:07,500
Sound advice, Uncle.
Thank you.

55
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:11,010
Always so stiff, like a board.

56
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:13,380
That is your
defining characteristic.

57
00:02:13,430 --> 00:02:15,130
-[XYLO] Your Eminence.
-[MARLEN] Hm?

58
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:16,300
Xylo! Be quiet!

59
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:18,970
What I have to say
should be of use.

60
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:20,430
It's imperative.

61
00:02:20,470 --> 00:02:23,390
Otherwise, I would never
interrupt a man of your status.

62
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:24,600
[Marlen chuckles]

63
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:28,150
An assertive tone delivering
words of conciliation.

64
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,570
-Patausche...
-[KIVIA] Uh?

65
00:02:29,610 --> 00:02:31,570
[MARLEN]...you could
learn from this man.

66
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,700
[KIVIA] Right, understood.

67
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:36,530
[MARLEN] You have
my attention, Hero Xylo.

68
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:39,620
Please enlighten us
with your insight.

69
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:43,040
[XYLO] Eminence, we should start
by investigating the middleman.

70
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:45,830
Such as those
in the Adventurers Guild.

71
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:48,460
♪

72
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,550
[XYLO] Lideo Sodrick.

73
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:57,390
So I take it this guy's
the guildmaster?

74
00:02:57,430 --> 00:02:59,430
[SIENA] They say
an ancestor of his

75
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:00,680
founded a private army

76
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:03,430
to take down the pirates
plaguing Korio Bay.

77
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:06,440
And that's how
the guild came to be.

78
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,810
It's a nice little
bedtime story.

79
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:10,730
But it was probably
just a turf war

80
00:03:10,770 --> 00:03:12,360
between wannabe pirates.

81
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,990
Well, be that as it may be,

82
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:16,320
this Lideo Sodrick
is a big deal.

83
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:19,030
The history
of the Sodrick's Shell region

84
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:21,120
and that of the
Adventurers Guild

85
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,950
are one and the same.

86
00:03:25,370 --> 00:03:27,120
[footsteps]

87
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,840
-[VENETIM] Back at last.
-[XYLO] Huh?

88
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,050
Any cause for concern?

89
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:36,300
Huh? What do you mean?

90
00:03:36,340 --> 00:03:37,840
[VENETIM] Well, it's just...

91
00:03:37,890 --> 00:03:39,800
I figured they might have
saddled us

92
00:03:39,850 --> 00:03:41,970
with a new punishment
or some such.

93
00:03:42,010 --> 00:03:43,260
-[snoring]
-[BOTH] Uh?

94
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,230
[snores]

95
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:49,480
No need to worry.

96
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,980
It was all surprisingly
reasonable.

97
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:53,820
You don't say.

98
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:55,110
Problem?

99
00:03:55,150 --> 00:03:57,070
Don't tell me
you're nursing the dream

100
00:03:57,110 --> 00:03:59,320
of making a pass
at that sniper lady.

101
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:00,490
Of course not!

102
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:02,700
It isn't anything of the sort.

103
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:03,990
I...

104
00:04:04,330 --> 00:04:05,540
Actually...

105
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:07,040
Forget I said anything.

106
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,710
So dramatic.

107
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:10,580
[Dotta groans]

108
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:13,800
Help me pick our mission's crew.

109
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,220
I'll give you a few pointers
while we're at it.

110
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:17,470
How generous.

111
00:04:17,550 --> 00:04:19,680
But I assure you I don't need
any such advice.

112
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:21,220
[Xylo chuckles]

113
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:24,100
It has nothing to do
with romance.

114
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:28,310
I swear,
it's completely unrelated.

115
00:04:31,810 --> 00:04:34,270
[LIDEO] I'm appalled
by your utter failure.

116
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:36,280
We weren't expecting a dragon,

117
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:37,820
and the heroes
were much stronger

118
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,700
than our intel
led us to believe.

119
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:42,570
By the way, that man
is an amateur.

120
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:45,790
You should take him off the job
or kill him where he stands.

121
00:04:45,830 --> 00:04:47,250
Are you referring to me?

122
00:04:47,330 --> 00:04:51,080
I had stumbled across Boojum
at a gambling house I oversee.

123
00:04:51,130 --> 00:04:53,290
The place was drenched in blood.

124
00:04:53,590 --> 00:04:56,420
Ten adventurers there
decided to gang up on him.

125
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:58,470
He killed every last one.

126
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:05,010
If he's such an amateur,
teach him what he needs to know.

127
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:07,470
[SHIJI BAU] Mm... He'll make
things even harder.

128
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:09,850
I'll need a bigger payday
for all that.

129
00:05:09,890 --> 00:05:11,190
[Lideo scoffs]

130
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:14,440
Claiming the enemy's too strong
is an excuse to beg for money.

131
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,660
I see your game.

132
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:25,490
You're deliberately trying
to provoke me.

133
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:28,410
Big brother,
this woman is a wild dog.

134
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:31,250
A masterless beast
is dangerous.

135
00:05:31,290 --> 00:05:33,710
[LIDEO] Iri, stand down.

136
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:35,380
I'll be fine.

137
00:05:37,590 --> 00:05:40,760
[LIDEO] Shiji Bau, you're in
the Adventurers Guild now,

138
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,010
not the military.

139
00:05:43,890 --> 00:05:46,850
If you quit early, you won't get
your final payout.

140
00:05:46,890 --> 00:05:49,890
[grunts] This better be
a third of what's on the way.

141
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:55,860
I'll hire my own people.
Pros, for a change.

142
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,190
You dare?

143
00:05:57,230 --> 00:05:59,730
[BOOJUM] I'd also like
a small pay increase.

144
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:02,570
I would like to purchase
another book.

145
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:05,490
I quite enjoy this writer

146
00:06:05,910 --> 00:06:07,660
Altoyard Comette.

147
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:10,750
He's a rather brilliant poet.

148
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:18,300
[IRI] Brother,
do you think they can do it?

149
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:21,800
That is not something you need
to worry yourself about.

150
00:06:26,550 --> 00:06:29,220
Do you sense someone's
presence out there?

151
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:33,890
[birds chirping]

152
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:37,480
[snores softly]

153
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:39,480
♪

154
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:43,490
[yawns]

155
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:46,570
[XYLO] Huh?

156
00:06:48,410 --> 00:06:50,660
I'm not used to
seeing you up this early.

157
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:53,330
Guessing Neely kicked you
out of the stables?

158
00:06:53,370 --> 00:06:54,620
-She did.
-[XYLO] Huh?

159
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:56,670
She's got a jealous streak,

160
00:06:56,710 --> 00:06:59,630
and caught me spending time
with another dragon.

161
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:02,550
But it wasn't even like that.

162
00:07:02,590 --> 00:07:03,760
Just drop it.

163
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:06,300
It's too early to listen
to you two bicker.

164
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:08,140
You guys
just take any excuse

165
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:09,640
to pick a fight with each other.

166
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,010
That's an exaggeration.

167
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,470
No, it isn't.

168
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:14,850
You're like powder kegs
of rage and violence

169
00:07:14,890 --> 00:07:16,480
always on the verge
of exploding.

170
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,270
-I don't get why they don't...
-Are those three heroes?

171
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:19,810
...at least put you
on different meal schedules.

172
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:22,150
I recognize the shifty one.
It's Xylo Forbartz.

173
00:07:22,190 --> 00:07:24,690
[DOTTA] Where's Teoritta?
Did you ditch her?

174
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:26,410
She's still sleeping.

175
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:30,120
Besides, I can't let her hear
what I'm about to say.

176
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,870
Uh-oh, I know that look.

177
00:07:32,910 --> 00:07:34,870
You're gonna try and make me
do something.

178
00:07:34,910 --> 00:07:36,120
You're right.

179
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,330
And it's something
really dangerous, yeah?

180
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,670
And way too dangerous

181
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:41,540
for the little goddess
to tag along.

182
00:07:41,590 --> 00:07:44,210
Well done.
We're on the same page.

183
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:45,590
[Dotta groans]

184
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:47,380
You should be excited about it.

185
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:50,220
You'll get to walk around town
without shackles.

186
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:52,010
[DOTTA]
That doesn't mean anything.

187
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,220
Heard Tsav's right arm
got mangled in a fight

188
00:07:54,270 --> 00:07:56,520
during his leisurely stroll
in town.

189
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,690
[XYLO] That's true,

190
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:00,400
and he should thank his
lucky stars it was just an arm.

191
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,940
[DOTTA] I'm scared to ask,
but what's the plan?

192
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:05,570
[XYLO] We'll start
by infiltrating

193
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:07,070
the Adventurers Guild.

194
00:08:07,610 --> 00:08:09,030
[DOTTA]
But wouldn't Rhyno make

195
00:08:09,070 --> 00:08:10,820
a much better fake adventurer
than me?

196
00:08:10,870 --> 00:08:12,910
He used to actually
be one, right?

197
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:14,240
[XYLO] Not an option.

198
00:08:14,290 --> 00:08:15,660
He's locked up at the moment,

199
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:18,120
and he's much too unpredictable
for this mission.

200
00:08:18,170 --> 00:08:19,290
[SOLDIER]
Couldn't agree more.

201
00:08:19,330 --> 00:08:21,500
Why not an ace liar
like Venetim, huh?

202
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:23,960
He's with His Majesty
at the repair shop.

203
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,630
Seems they finally found
the king a replacement leg.

204
00:08:26,670 --> 00:08:29,630
-There's gotta be someone else.
-[objects clattering]

205
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:31,720
[JAYCE]
If Dotta won't go, I'll do it.

206
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,430
Got nothin' better to do.

207
00:08:33,470 --> 00:08:35,220
Whoa! You mean it?

208
00:08:35,270 --> 00:08:36,600
Well, then...

209
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:40,400
Dotta, I need
your unique skillset.

210
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:43,690
[sighs] I give up.

211
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:47,900
[scoffs] You had better not
stir up any trouble for Dotta.

212
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:51,070
He gave his arm
to feed a hungry dragon.

213
00:08:51,110 --> 00:08:54,030
That's how incredible
of a human being he is.

214
00:08:54,370 --> 00:08:57,410
I'm not even sure
I could make the sacrifice.

215
00:08:58,580 --> 00:08:59,750
[Dotta groans]

216
00:08:59,790 --> 00:09:02,540
You have
an unconventional admirer.

217
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:04,420
I don't wanna talk about it.

218
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:07,210
Go on. Tell me everything.

219
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:09,590
How do you plan
to infiltrate the guild?

220
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,010
[XYLO] It's simple.

221
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,260
♪

222
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:15,550
[Dotta] Uh...

223
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:18,140
[Xylo grunts]

224
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:21,350
[KIVIA] Hmm.

225
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:24,650
Is there a problem, Xylo?

226
00:09:24,690 --> 00:09:27,150
Do you think
I look mannish again?

227
00:09:27,820 --> 00:09:29,440
Say it. I dare you.

228
00:09:29,490 --> 00:09:30,610
[Dotta grunts nervously]

229
00:09:30,650 --> 00:09:33,070
[Xylo sighs]

230
00:09:33,610 --> 00:09:35,740
No. The dress suits you.

231
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:38,370
You're the spitting image
of a young noblewoman,

232
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:41,210
with a string of suitors
fawning over her.

233
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:42,790
[Kivia gasps]

234
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:45,920
I despise empty flattery!

235
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,260
You can't compliment your way
to my good side.

236
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:51,130
That will never work.
I am indomitable.

237
00:09:51,170 --> 00:09:52,840
Glad to hear it.

238
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:55,050
Now then, what's our reason
for hiring them?

239
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:56,300
[Kivia clears throat]

240
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,560
[KIVIA]
For such an establishment,

241
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:00,730
requesting faerie hunting
might work.

242
00:10:00,770 --> 00:10:03,690
And here I thought that was
the military's job.

243
00:10:03,730 --> 00:10:06,310
We could ask them to take out
some bandits.

244
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:08,730
Can we not minimize
the scale of violence

245
00:10:08,780 --> 00:10:09,940
at least a little bit?

246
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:12,740
Bandit hunting may have worked
if we were out in the sticks,

247
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:14,320
but instead, we're in Ioff City.

248
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,030
[KIVIA] Why don't you
go ahead and tell us

249
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:18,240
your brilliant suggestion?

250
00:10:18,290 --> 00:10:19,490
[DOTTA] Hmm.

251
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:25,130
Well, maybe, you're
a cold nobleman's wife.

252
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:27,000
And you're her secret lover.

253
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:28,250
-[KIVIA] I'm what?
-[XYLO] Huh?

254
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:31,050
And you're plotting
to get her husband murdered.

255
00:10:31,090 --> 00:10:34,380
Any nobles out there
you want gone, for good?

256
00:10:36,930 --> 00:10:39,350
[CONFESSOR]
Defendant: Dotta Luzulas,

257
00:10:39,390 --> 00:10:42,520
you've managed to amass
over a thousand criminal acts

258
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:43,940
on your record.

259
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:45,730
[DOTTA] Uh...

260
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:47,690
[CONFESSOR] Yet, you've been
brought before us today

261
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:49,690
to answer for just one of them.

262
00:10:49,730 --> 00:10:51,490
While escaping
the castle dungeon

263
00:10:51,530 --> 00:10:53,070
in which you were confined,

264
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:56,320
you attempted to steal
a dragon from the stables.

265
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:01,290
[DOTTA] Uh, wait,
something's not right.

266
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:03,620
-[CONFESSOR] Elaborate.
-[DOTTA] What about him?

267
00:11:03,660 --> 00:11:05,960
I would have thought he was
the biggest part of my crime.

268
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,290
[CONFESSOR]
To whom are you referring?

269
00:11:07,330 --> 00:11:09,420
You know, I mean
the crown prince!

270
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:11,460
[NOBLE 1] What's he saying
about the crown prince?

271
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:13,420
[NOBLE 2] Why drag
His Highness into this?

272
00:11:13,470 --> 00:11:14,880
You're not listening.

273
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:17,010
That little boy asked me
to save his life.

274
00:11:17,050 --> 00:11:18,220
I'm not lying!

275
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:20,510
He told me he'd been
locked up in the castle,

276
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:22,060
that he needed to escape.

277
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:24,560
So I swiped the dragon
to help him break free and--

278
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,520
[CONFESSOR]
I've heard enough of your lies.

279
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,940
[Dotta gasps]

280
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:29,860
[CONFESSOR]
Your fantastical assertion

281
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:31,480
that the crown prince
spoke to you

282
00:11:31,530 --> 00:11:33,030
is unequivocally false.

283
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:36,110
As is your claim that he
attempted to escape the castle.

284
00:11:36,150 --> 00:11:38,740
No. There's gotta be
some mistake.

285
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:40,910
It was just after
I broke out of my cell.

286
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:44,330
I know it was the First Prince
of the Federated Kingdom.

287
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:48,750
He was only ten or so,
and the boy was terrified.

288
00:11:48,790 --> 00:11:50,840
He said his family changed.

289
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:53,170
That the king wasn't behaving
like himself.

290
00:11:53,210 --> 00:11:55,260
-And I think the chancellor--
-[CONFESSOR] Silence!

291
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:57,050
You've said your piece.

292
00:11:57,090 --> 00:11:58,390
[DOTTA] No, wait.

293
00:11:58,430 --> 00:12:01,180
There's something going on
with the royal family!

294
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:02,560
It's all true!

295
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,640
Why else would the crown prince
ask a thief for help?

296
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:07,810
A two-bit scumbag like me.

297
00:12:07,850 --> 00:12:10,810
I'm... nothing. Nobody.

298
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,520
[CONFESSOR] I said be silent!

299
00:12:12,570 --> 00:12:15,280
But even an actual lowlife
like me has a conscience.

300
00:12:15,690 --> 00:12:17,030
There aren't
a whole lot of people

301
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:18,700
who can draw it out of me.

302
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:21,700
But when I see someone
weaker than I am,

303
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,580
like the prince was
in that moment,

304
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:26,580
I just wanna help them,
like anyone would.

305
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:27,960
[screams]

306
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,130
None of this is right.

307
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,050
Lock me up. Fine.

308
00:12:36,090 --> 00:12:38,380
But someone has to
save the prince!

309
00:12:38,430 --> 00:12:39,800
I beg you.

310
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:42,100
Someone help the prince
before it's too late!

311
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:44,760
[CONFESSOR] We cannot continue
the trial like this.

312
00:12:44,810 --> 00:12:47,390
[BAILIFF] Lord Confessor,
I believe death would be

313
00:12:47,430 --> 00:12:49,270
a reasonable sentence
in this case?

314
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,020
[CONFESSOR] Yes,
that's certainly true.

315
00:12:51,610 --> 00:12:54,520
But an even harsher punishment
has already been approved

316
00:12:54,570 --> 00:12:56,070
for the guilty party.

317
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:58,700
[BAILIFF] May I ask by whom?

318
00:12:58,740 --> 00:13:00,570
[CONFESSOR]
That suggestion was made

319
00:13:00,610 --> 00:13:02,660
by the Central Noble Alliance.

320
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:04,660
The decision is final.

321
00:13:06,450 --> 00:13:07,620
[DOTTA] Monsters!

322
00:13:07,750 --> 00:13:09,910
I swear I'll steal the prince
no matter what!

323
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:13,750
[CONFESSOR] Dotta Luzulas,
you are hereby sentenced

324
00:13:13,790 --> 00:13:15,880
to serve as a hero.

325
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:22,050
[Dotta sighs]

326
00:13:22,470 --> 00:13:24,100
Really don't wanna be here.

327
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:27,220
But I guess I've got no choice.

328
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:29,600
[footsteps]

329
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:38,650
[MAN 1]
Hey, check out my wares!

330
00:13:38,690 --> 00:13:40,320
[MAN 2]
You want a drag?

331
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,360
-[MAN 1] They're ignoring us.
-[MAN 2] Swine.

332
00:13:42,910 --> 00:13:45,280
Well, this is unpleasant.
[coughs]

333
00:13:45,330 --> 00:13:46,370
[lecherous chuckling]

334
00:13:46,410 --> 00:13:48,240
[XYLO] It's called
"Dragon's Breath."

335
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,910
You can thank Jayce
for its popularity.

336
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:53,710
They are brazenly
breaking the law.

337
00:13:56,590 --> 00:13:57,840
[XYLO] I'm curious.

338
00:13:57,880 --> 00:14:00,340
What made you
want to join the military?

339
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:03,340
Why ask?

340
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:06,100
You're from a Temple family
with a large domain.

341
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:08,850
It doesn't make sense
to put your neck on the line.

342
00:14:09,930 --> 00:14:11,140
Guess not.

343
00:14:12,690 --> 00:14:15,230
[KIVIA] Both, my mother
and father are priests.

344
00:14:15,270 --> 00:14:16,980
They carried out
important duties

345
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:18,110
for the Temple

346
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:20,230
earning them certain benefits.

347
00:14:20,650 --> 00:14:22,110
[XYLO] "Benefits."

348
00:14:22,150 --> 00:14:26,240
Noble Priests seeking influence,
cashing in on their faith.

349
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:27,780
Right.

350
00:14:27,830 --> 00:14:29,910
And not always through
aboveboard methods

351
00:14:29,950 --> 00:14:31,410
like donations.

352
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:33,210
I hated that about them

353
00:14:33,250 --> 00:14:35,460
and wanted to walk
a different path.

354
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,210
So I joined the military,

355
00:14:37,250 --> 00:14:38,840
hoping to make my own way,

356
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:41,170
through my own hard work.

357
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:46,140
[XYLO] Hm? Kivia?

358
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:48,850
This training sword
is the first I ever owned.

359
00:14:49,850 --> 00:14:51,810
My uncle bought it for me.

360
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,890
I wanted my own future,

361
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:58,270
secured with nothing more
than my own talent.

362
00:14:58,310 --> 00:15:02,690
My uncle has supported me
in that endeavor, always.

363
00:15:05,610 --> 00:15:07,870
[clears throat]
Your turn to share.

364
00:15:07,910 --> 00:15:10,370
Let's see. So, um...

365
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:12,200
-Your fiancée--
-[DOTTA] Xylo!

366
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:14,540
I finished scouting the guild.

367
00:15:15,290 --> 00:15:17,830
[XYLO] That was fast.
Good work.

368
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,880
[KIVIA] Honestly,
maybe a little too fast.

369
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:22,630
The security over there
seems pretty tight.

370
00:15:22,670 --> 00:15:24,970
I think I spotted
around 20 guards.

371
00:15:25,010 --> 00:15:26,300
[XYLO] Less than expected.

372
00:15:26,340 --> 00:15:29,180
There's more.
I saw a bunch of kids around.

373
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:31,140
Little assassins or something.

374
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,890
Children?

375
00:15:32,930 --> 00:15:34,480
That's heinous.

376
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:35,980
[XYLO]
I've heard the rumors.

377
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:39,360
They take in orphans and
raise them into loyal soldiers

378
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,860
who do their bidding.

379
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,490
All of that aside,

380
00:15:44,650 --> 00:15:46,910
you really want me
to kidnap the guildmaster

381
00:15:46,950 --> 00:15:48,660
while you're distracting
everyone?

382
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:50,200
You realize
that stealing people

383
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,910
has never gone
very well for me?

384
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:53,410
Figure it out.

385
00:15:53,450 --> 00:15:54,540
Ready?

386
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:56,870
You are the daughter
of a wealthy nobleman.

387
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:59,170
And I'm your secret lover.

388
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,590
Sure! No problem!
Leave it to me!

389
00:16:02,630 --> 00:16:03,590
[Xylo grunts]

390
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:05,550
[XYLO] Not so rough.

391
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:12,010
[IRI] He appears to be
that penal hero, Xylo Forbartz.

392
00:16:12,050 --> 00:16:13,680
There's a woman with him, too.

393
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:15,850
She's clearly a Holy Knight.

394
00:16:16,230 --> 00:16:18,140
Xylo Forbartz, huh?

395
00:16:18,190 --> 00:16:19,600
That isn't good.

396
00:16:19,650 --> 00:16:22,480
Although, if we play
our cards right,

397
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:25,360
we might be able
to take him in alive.

398
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,990
Got it. I will find an opening.

399
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:31,620
Bring Shiji Bau and the rest.

400
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:34,620
Just in case,
wake up Duhrsami.

401
00:16:37,410 --> 00:16:39,250
Capture or kill them.

402
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:40,920
We won't fail.

403
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:42,630
[door closes]

404
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:44,800
[fire crackling]

405
00:16:51,180 --> 00:16:53,810
All of this is for my family.

406
00:16:54,890 --> 00:16:56,350
[indistinct chatter]

407
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,890
[receptionist yawning]

408
00:16:58,890 --> 00:17:00,850
-How's it goin'?
-No complaints here.

409
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:02,810
[RECEPTIONIST] Mmm?

410
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:07,740
There's someone
I want to make disappear.

411
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,490
[RECEPTIONIST] Huh?

412
00:17:09,530 --> 00:17:10,910
[KIVIA] I want the best.

413
00:17:10,950 --> 00:17:12,740
Someone with
a lot of experience.

414
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:15,740
I see. And you would be...

415
00:17:15,790 --> 00:17:17,660
You can call me Madleen, Miss.

416
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:19,580
Don't ask for my family name.

417
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:20,750
Right.

418
00:17:23,330 --> 00:17:26,380
[RECEPTIONIST] Very well,
I assume you have a reference?

419
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:29,470
So are you going
to take the job or aren't you?

420
00:17:29,510 --> 00:17:30,510
Tell me.

421
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:33,510
Miss Madleen,
we don't accept jobs

422
00:17:33,550 --> 00:17:35,850
from just anyone
who walks in the door.

423
00:17:35,890 --> 00:17:37,520
I apologize.

424
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:39,350
My lady is quite sheltered.

425
00:17:39,390 --> 00:17:41,440
This is all rather new to her.

426
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:44,560
We don't have a reference,
but we're desperate.

427
00:17:44,610 --> 00:17:46,690
At the least,
we need to leave town.

428
00:17:46,730 --> 00:17:48,690
Without being traced.

429
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:53,490
So hypothetically speaking,
who do you want killed?

430
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:55,910
A pesky nobleman.

431
00:17:55,950 --> 00:17:57,740
You know the Hystead family?

432
00:17:57,790 --> 00:17:59,410
Bridge-keepers of Ginai?

433
00:17:59,450 --> 00:18:00,540
I don't.

434
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:03,080
We are having trouble
with a third son

435
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,920
from one of their
branch families.

436
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:08,090
I had the misfortune
of marrying into that family.

437
00:18:08,130 --> 00:18:10,300
But then this man, and I...

438
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:12,220
We pledged body and soul
to each other

439
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:13,970
beneath a sacred hagra tree!

440
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:15,050
[RECEPTIONIST] Oh.

441
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:16,720
[KIVIA] That's why I want
my husband killed,

442
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:19,270
so I am free to live out my days
with my lover.

443
00:18:19,310 --> 00:18:22,690
Yes! Even if that means
running away together!

444
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:26,690
Got it. Just give me a minute,
all right? [sighs]

445
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:28,020
I've got a bad feeling.

446
00:18:28,110 --> 00:18:30,360
[KIVIA] I think they suspect
we're up to something.

447
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,150
[XYLO] Yeah,
that much is obvious.

448
00:18:32,190 --> 00:18:34,490
-[KIVIA] This is bad. What now?
-[indistinct chatter]

449
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,110
-[RECEPTIONIST] Truly doubt it.
-[XYLO] Here's a thought.

450
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,160
Raise hell.

451
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,160
[KIVIA] How so?

452
00:18:38,530 --> 00:18:40,490
[XYLO] We'll stir up
some trouble and cause chaos,

453
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:43,040
like setting a fire
to rob a place.

454
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,500
Although in our case,

455
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:46,460
we're here to steal
Lideo Sodrick.

456
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,960
[KIVIA] What? That plan is
absurdly reckless!

457
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,550
But we're still doing it.
Starting with them!

458
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,010
[XYLO] Uh...

459
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:57,340
You did request someone skilled
now, didn't you?

460
00:18:57,390 --> 00:18:58,930
-[Xylo gasps]
-It's you.

461
00:18:58,970 --> 00:19:00,850
Hello, Miss Renzari.

462
00:19:01,350 --> 00:19:03,810
It would seem we have
an enamored noblewoman

463
00:19:03,850 --> 00:19:06,270
and her paramour. Am I right?

464
00:19:06,310 --> 00:19:07,860
[Kivia and Xylo grunt softly]

465
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,990
[FRENCI]
May we borrow a room upstairs?

466
00:19:12,690 --> 00:19:14,700
♪

467
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:16,950
You are such a mess, Xylo.

468
00:19:16,990 --> 00:19:19,910
[grunts] I had a feeling
you would say that.

469
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:21,490
You're also stupid.

470
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:23,870
If I hadn't stepped in
to bail you out,

471
00:19:23,910 --> 00:19:26,210
you two would have
undoubtedly been arrested.

472
00:19:26,250 --> 00:19:28,130
[XYLO] You're wrong.
For your information,

473
00:19:28,170 --> 00:19:29,960
we were just about
to cause a commotion,

474
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,000
-so there...
-[KIVIA] True.

475
00:19:31,050 --> 00:19:32,760
Then our ally was to sneak in,

476
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:34,840
and secure us the evidence
that we need.

477
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:38,340
I'm curious.
Are you with the Holy Knights?

478
00:19:38,390 --> 00:19:41,510
Captain of the Thirteenth Order
of the Holy Knights.

479
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,270
Patausche Kivia.

480
00:19:43,310 --> 00:19:46,690
I would prefer if you
stopped indulging my fiancé.

481
00:19:46,730 --> 00:19:48,520
Seeing as how he's foolish,

482
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:52,150
lacking education, boorish,
as well as thoughtless...

483
00:19:52,190 --> 00:19:54,740
I don't need an outsider
egging him on.

484
00:19:54,780 --> 00:19:57,280
[KIVIA] An outsider?
That's quite rich.

485
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:59,120
You're the outsider
to this plan.

486
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,910
[FRENCI] I am his fiancée.

487
00:20:00,950 --> 00:20:03,660
We must face
all of life's trials together.

488
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:05,330
That's a sorry excuse!

489
00:20:09,210 --> 00:20:10,500
Here we go.

490
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:12,290
I had a feeling
your personalities

491
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:13,670
were doomed to clash,

492
00:20:13,710 --> 00:20:15,130
but not like this.

493
00:20:15,170 --> 00:20:17,090
What? Why would you say that?

494
00:20:17,130 --> 00:20:19,090
What's wrong
with our personalities?

495
00:20:19,140 --> 00:20:22,350
[FRENCI] You always come
to the most asinine conclusions.

496
00:20:22,390 --> 00:20:24,220
Is there no brain
between your ears?

497
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:26,430
[KIVIA] No. If only it were
that simple.

498
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:29,190
His mind is incapable
of accurately judging others.

499
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:30,310
[FRENCI] I agree.

500
00:20:30,730 --> 00:20:33,110
His observational skills
are on par with a susubana mole.

501
00:20:33,150 --> 00:20:35,480
[KIVIA] I would go so far
as to say your average tree

502
00:20:35,530 --> 00:20:36,650
is smarter than him.

503
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:39,740
[XYLO] Can you please stop
bonding over insulting me?

504
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:42,780
We've got a serious situation
on our hands.

505
00:20:43,490 --> 00:20:44,660
That's better.

506
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:46,240
Now, why are you here?

507
00:20:46,290 --> 00:20:49,500
[FRENCI] I'm investigating,
disguised as an adventurer.

508
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:51,460
I was on the verge
of finally making contact

509
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,750
with Lideo Sodrick
until you arrived.

510
00:20:53,790 --> 00:20:56,010
[XYLO] Sorry we messed that up
for you.

511
00:20:56,050 --> 00:20:58,420
Although, perhaps
we could just combine our...

512
00:20:58,470 --> 00:21:00,760
-[knocks on door]
-[GIRL] Excuse the interruption.

513
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:03,100
The Guildmaster would like
to speak with you

514
00:21:03,140 --> 00:21:04,970
about your job request.

515
00:21:05,350 --> 00:21:09,480
[Xylo chuckles]
Frenci, feel free to back out.

516
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:10,730
You jest.

517
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:12,770
The very notion disgusts me.

518
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:20,530
I knew this would end with us
stirring things up.

519
00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:31,830
-[sword slashes]
-[gasps]

520
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:37,170
[screams]

521
00:21:40,010 --> 00:21:41,050
Little lout.

522
00:21:42,090 --> 00:21:43,260
Mind your manners.

523
00:22:01,650 --> 00:22:04,160
[mercenary grunting]

524
00:22:16,130 --> 00:22:17,340
Drop something?

525
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:23,340
[mercenary gasps]

526
00:22:23,840 --> 00:22:25,800
[all yelling]

527
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:28,180
[grunts]

528
00:22:28,220 --> 00:22:31,100
[all screaming]

529
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:34,690
[Xylo laughs]
We caused some solid chaos.

530
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:41,070
This isn't how I foresaw
the mission going.

531
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:43,740
My goodness.
You're going through with it.

532
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:44,820
Right.

533
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:47,870
We have a chance
to smoke out Lideo Sodrick,

534
00:22:47,910 --> 00:22:50,290
and clean up the town
while we're at it.

535
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:52,660
Seriously?

536
00:22:52,710 --> 00:22:55,460
Think of it as our civic duty.

537
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:58,040
No way this turns out well.

538
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:03,260
[♪ closing theme song playing]
